            <ArticleTitle>Imaging of tarsal navicular stress injury with a focus on MRI: A pictorial essay.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>359-64</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/1754-9485.12435</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Predominantly diagnosed in athletes, stress fracture of the tarsal navicular is becoming increasingly recognised by clinicians as a cause of midfoot pain. Delayed diagnosis can increase the significant morbidity associated with this condition. Consequently the role of MRI is increasing, given the potential to identify a stress reaction in the navicular prior to the development of a discrete stress fracture. It is necessary for radiologists to be familiar with the typical and atypical appearances of this important condition.</AbstractText>
